  "aboutWarningTitle": "Important: observing and interpreting the body signs",
  "aboutWarningBody": "Reliable cycle tracking depends on the faithful observation and interpretation of the body signs (temperature, mucus). The guide by Prof. Rötzer or a course (see INER) teaches the skills needed. Bring your questions to INER (iner.org).",
  "@aboutWarningBody": {
    "description": "First-start warning: reliable tracking requires the faithful observation and interpretation of the body signs; the Rötzer guide / INER courses teach the skills, INER answers questions. INER's website (iner.org) is named as plain, copyable text — the link handling is a later concern."
  },
  "aboutPosture": "The app supports — it never decides: it computes and displays, but gives no fertility verdict; the evaluation stays with you.",
  "aboutPrivacyHeading": "Privacy",
  "@aboutPrivacyHeading": {
    "description": "Heading of the GDPR notice on the about/onboarding page and the title of the settings pane's privacy card — one string on both surfaces."
  },
  "aboutPrivacyBody": "This app stores all data exclusively locally on your device. On Android and iOS the database is stored encrypted; its key lives in the system's protected storage. The browser storage of the web build (OPFS/IndexedDB) is not encrypted by the app — the web build serves development only. There are no servers, no cloud, no analytics services. Your data is never sent — not even on a crash or an error. Data leaves the device only when you yourself create and share an export/backup file. No personal data is transmitted to third parties. You can exercise your GDPR rights (e.g. access, deletion) directly within the app: view via Settings › Export, deletion via Delete data, restore via Import.",
  "@aboutPrivacyBody": {
    "description": "GDPR/privacy notice, English mirror of the German original — no servers, no transmission, crash-safe; the encryption claim is platform-qualified: Android/iOS databases are encrypted at rest (key in the system's protected storage, ADR-0005), while the web build's browser storage (OPFS/IndexedDB) is NOT encrypted by the app (web stays an unencrypted development tool). GDPR rights referenced to the in-app actions (export view/delete-data/import)."
  },
  "aboutContinue": "Continue",
  "aboutLicenseHeading": "License",
  "aboutLicenseBody": "© 2026 Benedikt Burger — Apache-2.0. Further license texts — for bundled fonts and the Flutter engine — and the licenses of the used pub packages are readable in-app under License details. The repository (github.com/BenediktBurger/cycle-app) is a further reference.",
  "@aboutLicenseBody": {
    "description": "License/copyright section, English mirror of the German: the chosen license (Apache-2.0, set 2026-09) and its copyright holder. Further license texts — e.g. for bundled fonts and the Flutter engine — and the licenses of the used pub packages are readable in-app via the license-details row (offline redistribution obligations, ADR-0011): the build auto-collects the packages' license texts (NOTICES), the bundled font's license ships as an asset. The body deliberately does not enumerate individual licenses because their texts ship in the binary; the repository is the additional, deeper reference (full sources), not a substitute for the in-app texts."
  },
  "aboutLicenseDetailsRow": "License details",
  "@aboutLicenseDetailsRow": {
    "description": "Tappable row label after the license/copyright section: opens the in-app license page showing the bundled license texts (the app's Apache-2.0 and the Noto Sans font license)."
  },
  "aboutBackupHint": "Backup, moving to another device, and recovery work only through the JSON export/import in the settings — the database file itself cannot be copied, because its key is bound to this device.",
  "@aboutBackupHint": {
    "description": "One-sentence backup hint on the about/onboarding page, English mirror of the German (settingsExportNote's backup role): export/import is the only backup/migration/recovery path; copying the encrypted, device-bound database file is never usable (ADR-0005)."
  },
